      "id": 85902,
      "name": "Envisioner",
      "username": "Envisioner",
      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/e/9de053/{size}.png",
      "created_at": "2014-01-08T07:00:32.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>The one thing that bothers me is that not all of the effects say \"You may use a power NOW\", which leads to situations where the pedant in me wants to know whether I'm supposed to wait and use the power during the current turn's power phase.&nbsp; Overdrive is one of the cards that bothers me on this level; nothing about the way it's worded implies that if Argent Adept grants him a card play with Silver Shadow + Inventive Preparation, and he plays Overdrive, that he'd Strike twice <em>immediately</em>, as it's just saying he can do so \"this turn\".&nbsp; That implies he'd have to observe the normal rule that Powers are used during the power phase, even if it breaks the rule that it usually has to be <em>your</em> power phase.</p>",
      "post_number": 4,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:09:43.731Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
      "quote_count": 0,
      "incoming_link_count": 0,
