    {
      "id": 85904,
      "name": "phantaskippy",
      "username": "phantaskippy",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/phantaskippy/{size}/1897_2.png",
      "created_at": "2014-01-08T12:28:00.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Unlike Embolden Overdrive does not state you do it during the power phase.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>There is no inherent restriction on when you are allowed to do certain activities.</p><p>When Reset says to draw a card we don't wait until the draw phase, and no one questions Team leader letting you draw during the Power Phase or Adept letting you play a card during his power phase, but when powers get involved we start inventing restrictions.</p><p>The power phase is the point during your turn when you get a free power use. &nbsp;Just like the play phase and the draw phase.</p><p>Overdrive lets you use Strike twice during the current turn. &nbsp;That would fit anywhere between the start and end of turn.</p><p>&nbsp;</p>",
      "post_number": 6,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:09:43.880Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
